(CHAPTER 1: DATA PREPROCESSING & PRINCIPAL COMPONENT ANALYSIS \(Page 1\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 1: EDA & Feature Engineering · Section 1.1 · Page 1]) Tj T*
(Exploratory Data Analysis \(EDA\) inspects distributions and relationships before) Tj T*
(modeling.) Tj T*
(The Interquartile Range \(IQR\) equals Q3 - Q1, spanning the middle 50% of the) Tj T*
(distribution. Tukey outlier fences identify data points falling below Q1 - 1.5 * IQR) Tj T*
(or above Q3 + 1.5 * IQR as outliers. Extreme outliers lie beyond 3.0 * IQR.) Tj T*
(Missing data mechanisms fall into three categories:) Tj T*
(1. Missing Completely at Random \(MCAR\): Missingness is independent of both observed) Tj T*
(and unobserved variables.) Tj T*
(2. Missing at Random \(MAR\): Missingness is systematically related to observed) Tj T*
(variables, but not the missing value itself.) Tj T*
(3. Missing Not at Random \(MNAR\): Missingness depends directly on the unobserved) Tj T*
(missing value \(e.g., highest earners refusing to report income\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 1: EDA & Feature Engineering · Section 1.2 · Page 1]) Tj T*
(Feature scaling aligns variable magnitudes before gradient-based optimization or) Tj T*
(distance metrics:) Tj T*
(- Min-Max Normalization: x_norm = \(x - x_min\) / \(x_max - x_min\), binding values to [0,) Tj T*
(1]. Highly sensitive to outliers.) Tj T*
(- Standard Z-Score Standardization: x_std = \(x - mu\) / sigma, centering at zero mean) Tj T*
(with unit standard deviation. Preferred for algorithms assuming normal distribution) Tj T*
(\(Linear models, PCA, Logistic Regression\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 1: EDA & Feature Engineering · Section 1.3 · Page 1]) Tj T*
(Principal Component Analysis \(PCA\) is an unsupervised linear dimensionality reduction) Tj T*
(technique that maximizes variance while minimizing reconstruction error:) Tj T*
(1. Standardize the data matrix X \(n observations, p features\) so each feature has mean) Tj T*
(0 and variance 1.) Tj T*
(2. Compute the p x p sample covariance matrix: Sigma = \(1 / \(n - 1\)\) * X^T * X.) Tj T*
(3. Calculate the eigenvalues lambda_i and eigenvectors v_i of Sigma: Sigma * v_i =) Tj T*
(lambda_i * v_i.) Tj T*
(4. Sort eigenvectors in descending order of their eigenvalues. The first principal) Tj T*
(component PC1 points in the direction of maximum variance.) Tj T*
(5. The Explained Variance Ratio for component k is lambda_k / sum\(lambda_i\). The scree) Tj T*
(plot visualizes the cumulative variance explained to select the number of components.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
