(CHAPTER 2: REGRESSION, REGULARIZATION & ENSEMBLE TREES \(Page 2\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 2: Supervised Learning · Section 2.1 · Page 2]) Tj T*
(Ordinary Least Squares \(OLS\) regression models continuous targets: y = X * beta +) Tj T*
(epsilon.) Tj T*
(The Gauss-Markov theorem states that under five classic assumptions \(linearity in) Tj T*
(parameters, strict exogeneity E[epsilon|X] = 0, no perfect multicollinearity,) Tj T*
(homoscedasticity Var\(epsilon|X\) = sigma^2, and no autocorrelation\), the OLS estimator) Tj T*
(beta_hat = \(X^T * X\)^\(-1\) * X^T * y is the Best Linear Unbiased Estimator \(BLUE\).) Tj T*
(Multicollinearity occurs when predictor variables are highly correlated, causing \(X^T) Tj T*
(* X\) to become ill-conditioned, inflating standard errors of coefficients. It is) Tj T*
(diagnosed using the Variance Inflation Factor: VIF_j = 1 / \(1 - R_j^2\). A VIF > 5 to) Tj T*
(10 indicates severe multicollinearity.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 2: Supervised Learning · Section 2.2 · Page 2]) Tj T*
(Regularization prevents overfitting by penalizing large coefficient magnitudes:) Tj T*
(- Ridge Regression \(L2 penalty\): Minimizes ||y - X*beta||^2 + lambda * sum\(beta_j^2\).) Tj T*
(Shrinks coefficients toward zero, handling multicollinearity, but retains all features) Tj T*
(\(no sparsity\).) Tj T*
(- Lasso Regression \(L1 penalty\): Minimizes ||y - X*beta||^2 + lambda * sum\(|beta_j|\).) Tj T*
(The sharp diamond geometry of the L1 ball drives non-informative feature weights) Tj T*
(strictly to zero, performing automated feature selection.) Tj T*
(- ElasticNet combines both penalties: lambda_1 * ||beta||_1 + lambda_2 * ||beta||_2^2,) Tj T*
(ideal when features are correlated in groups.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 2: Supervised Learning · Section 2.3 · Page 2]) Tj T*
(Tree ensembles improve predictive stability:) Tj T*
(- Random Forest applies Bootstrap Aggregation \(Bagging\) to decision trees. It trains B) Tj T*
(independent trees on bootstrapped data subsets, randomly selecting a subset of) Tj T*
(features \(sqrt\(p\)\) at each split. Averaging decorrelates individual trees and reduces) Tj T*
(model variance without increasing bias.) Tj T*
(- Gradient Boosted Decision Trees \(XGBoost, LightGBM\) build trees sequentially in a) Tj T*
(forward stage-wise manner, where each subsequent tree fits the negative gradient) Tj T*
(\(pseudo-residuals\) of the loss function with respect to the previous ensemble) Tj T*
(predictions.) Tj T*
ET
