(CHAPTER 4: UNSUPERVISED CLUSTERING & TIME SERIES ANALYSIS \(Page 4\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 4: Clustering & Time Series · Section 4.1 · Page 4]) Tj T*
(Unsupervised Clustering groups unlabeled data points based on geometric proximity.) Tj T*
(K-Means Clustering partitions n observations into k clusters by minimizing Within-) Tj T*
(Cluster Sum of Squares \(WCSS, or inertia\):) Tj T*
(WCSS = sum_i sum_{x in S_i} ||x - mu_i||^2) Tj T*
(Algorithm:) Tj T*
(1. Initialize k cluster centroids randomly \(or via K-Means++ to disperse initial) Tj T*
(centroids\).) Tj T*
(2. Assignment Step: Assign each observation to its closest centroid using Euclidean) Tj T*
(distance.) Tj T*
(3. Update Step: Recompute each centroid as the arithmetic mean of all assigned) Tj T*
(observations.) Tj T*
(4. Repeat until centroid coordinates converge.) Tj T*
(The optimal number of clusters k is determined via the Elbow Method \(identifying the) Tj T*
(point of diminishing WCSS returns\) and the Silhouette Score s\(i\) = \(b\(i\) - a\(i\)\) /) Tj T*
(max\(a\(i\), b\(i\)\), where a\(i\) is mean intra-cluster distance and b\(i\) is mean nearest-) Tj T*
(cluster distance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Chapter 4: Clustering & Time Series · Section 4.2 · Page 4]) Tj T*
(Time Series Analysis and Stationarity:) Tj T*
(A time series is weakly \(covariance\) stationary if:) Tj T*
(1. Mean is constant over time: E[Y_t] = mu for all t.) Tj T*
(2. Variance is constant over time: Var\(Y_t\) = sigma^2 for all t \(homoscedasticity\).) Tj T*
(3. Autocovariance depends only on the lag k, not time t: Cov\(Y_t, Y_{t-k}\) = gamma_k.) Tj T*
(Non-stationary series containing unit roots can produce spurious regressions. The) Tj T*
(Augmented Dickey-Fuller \(ADF\) test checks the null hypothesis that a unit root is) Tj T*
(present \(non-stationary\). If p-value < 0.05, the null hypothesis is rejected and the) Tj T*
(series is stationary. Differencing \(Y'_t = Y_t - Y_{t-1}\) transforms non-stationary) Tj T*
(series into stationary series for ARIMA modeling.) Tj T*
ET
